{"type":"message","id":"3beaed17","parentId":"82d11f88","timestamp":"2026-04-09T00:14:26.368Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The knowledge base listings show that the notes are actually just showing the first 20 items per page (pagination). But wait - these lists only show 20 items because of pagination. And the total counts shown are only for the first page. But the migration results earlier showed ~865 new notes were added. \n\nWait, the issue here is that the list API returns pagination with 20 items per page, and `total` refers to total on that page? No, looking at the API docs - `total` is the total count. But the knowledge bases show \"总数: 20, has_more: True\" - which suggests the total count from the API might actually be the count per page, not the full KB total.\n\n\nLooking at the API docs more carefully, each call returns a fixed 20 items per page along with `notes[]`, `has_more`, and `total`. So when it shows \"总数: 20, has_more: True\", the `total` is actually just the count of items on that page, not the full knowledge base total. The `has_more: True` indicates there are more pages to fetch.\n\nBut this seems odd—if the migration added around 865 notes to each knowledge base, why would the count still show 20? I'm wondering if there's a discrepancy between what the batch-add API reported as successful and what actually got stored, or maybe the `total` field isn't cumulative. Let me verify this by checking the full count across all pages. Actually, thinking about it more - each page returns `total` as that page's count (20), and `has_more` tells you if there's more. So \"总数: 20, has_more: True\" just means \"this page has 20 items, there are more pages\". The actual total would require fetching all pages.\n\nSo the knowledge bases aren't showing the full migrated content. Let me try to get a proper count by checking multiple pages or looking at the total from the API response differently.\n\nThe batch-add responses showed varying success counts across different knowledge bases, which suggests not all notes were successfully added. I should try a different approach - maybe use the recall endpoint to get a more complete picture of what's actually in each knowledge base, or do a proper paginated scan to see the full contents.\n\nLooking at the migration data more carefully, the batch-add responses indicated that each knowledge base received somewhere between 200-500 notes, but the listing API is only showing 20 items per page. I need to verify this by actually paginating through the results to see what's truly stored in each knowledge base. The knowledge bases might be returning different totals depending on their configuration or when they were last synced. Let me try using the recall function to search across all three knowledge bases and get a unified view of what's actually stored in each one.","thinkingSignature":"5ac85e9e649864dc0af5b23f11bf25ac6cf5bdcdb6f69cfbf2466e1814ce0154"},{"type":"text","text":"列表只显示第一页20条，让我用语义搜索快速摸底三个库的实际内容分布：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_2vbtjdycibqm_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"export GETNOTE_API_KEY=\"gk_live_79414cc5d34021a6.f48b009c9ed9470d05fbec8f4ef919f4d657e7a15d91347a\"\nexport GETNOTE_CLIENT_ID=\"cli_a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef90\"\n\necho \"=== 搜索三个知识库内容分布 ===\"\n\n# 搜索芯片相关\necho \"--- 芯片业务 (9YeBam0m) ---\"\nfor kw in \"半导体\" \"芯片\" \"中美\" \"制裁\" \"华为\" \"出口管制\" \"AI\" \"算力\"; do\n  count=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://openapi.biji.com/open/api/v1/resource/recall/knowledge\" \\\n    -H \"Authorization: $GETNOTE_API_KEY\" \\\n    -H \"X-Client-ID: $GETNOTE_CLIENT_ID\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d \"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"$kw\\\",\\\"topic_ids\\\":[\\\"9YeBam0m\\\"],\\\"top_k\\\":1}\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('data',{}).get('total',0))\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"?\")\n  echo \"  $kw: $count 条\"\ndone\n\n# 搜索家庭教育相关\necho \"\"\necho \"--- 家庭教育 (EJX1r7bn) ---\"\nfor kw in \"中考\" \"高考\" \"成都\" \"高中\" \"初中\" \"英语\" \"数学\" \"学习\" \"孩子\" \"教育\"; do\n  count=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://openapi.biji.com/open/api/v1/resource/recall/knowledge\" \\\n    -H \"Authorization: $GETNOTE_API_KEY\" \\\n    -H \"X-Client-ID: $GETNOTE_CLIENT_ID\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d \"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"$kw\\\",\\\"topic_ids\\\":[\\\"EJX1r7bn\\\"],\\\"top_k\\\":1}\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('data',{}).get('total',0))\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"?\")\n  echo \"  $kw: $count 条\"\ndone\n\n# 搜索OpenClaw相关\necho \"\"\necho \"--- OpenClaw使用 (G0P1Z51J) ---\"\nfor kw in \"OpenClaw\" \"prompt\" \"AI工具\" \"工作流\" \"skill\"; do\n  count=$(curl -s -X POST \"https://openapi.biji.com/open/api/v1/resource/recall/knowledge\" \\\n    -H \"Authorization: $GETNOTE_API_KEY\" \\\n    -H \"X-Client-ID: $GETNOTE_CLIENT_ID\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d \"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"$kw\\\",\\\"topic_ids\\\":[\\\"G0P1Z51J\\\"],\\\"top_k\\\":1}\" | python3 -c \"import sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d.get('data',{}).get('total',0))\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"?\")\n  echo \"  $kw: $count 条\"\ndone"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":57306,"output":1323,"cacheRead":40516,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":99145,"cost":{"input":0.0171918,"output":0.0015876,"cacheRead":0.00243096,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.02121036}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775693639381,"responseId":"06262247f3711d2ff014ad8163cc7b7d"}}
