{"type":"message","id":"f9230837","parentId":"ce52c818","timestamp":"2026-04-09T01:04:01.463Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The OSS upload returned a 403 error. This is likely because the signature or policy has expired or there's an issue with the upload format. \n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe I need to use the exact field order and format. Or perhaps the policy contains the exact filename so I can't change it.\n\nActually, looking at the policy more carefully, it contains `get_notes_prod/202604090903/getnotes_img_1a75beb6801163a0Sz0fKzE0.jpg` in the conditions. But I tried to upload to a different filename `getnotes_img_1a75beb6801163a0Sz0fKzE4.jpg`. \n\nI should stick with the original filename from the policy and try uploading again, but I'm realizing the actual file content needs to be sent directly in the POST request, not as a form field. The signature might also be failing because the key or policy has changed. Let me fetch a fresh token and attempt the upload once more.","thinkingSignature":"fdd0393725c8d7095b1be0dcbded6a166f611fe1c376b2d05ef0bdecf9b77e09"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_sz85k6atdkdg_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"export GETNOTE_API_KEY=\"gk_live_79414cc5d34021a6.f48b009c9ed9470d05fbec8f4ef919f4d657e7a15d91347a\"\nexport GETNOTE_CLIENT_ID=\"cli_a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678abcdef90\"\n\n# 重新获取上传凭证，用相同的文件名\ncurl -s \"https://openapi.biji.com/open/api/v1/resource/image/upload_token?mime_type=jpg&count=1\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: $GETNOTE_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"X-Client-ID: $GETNOTE_CLIENT_ID\" | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndata=d.get('data',{})\nprint('access_url:', data.get('access_url',''))\nprint('object_key:', data.get('object_key',''))\nprint('host:', data.get('host',''))\nprint('signature:', data.get('signature',''))\nprint('policy:', data.get('policy','')[:50]+'...')\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2